# OpenCode iOS port patch -- 0009
# Title: iOS/Node 18 fallback: direct node:child_process standalone server spawn
# Upstream: anomalyco/opencode @ e8238bae9b807b72ecfc75afd3a9fe2e6b07b944 (v2.2.5)
# Requires: patches 0001-0008 applied first.
# Files: packages/cli/src/services/standalone.ts
# Why: on the device Node 18.20.4 runtime, `opencode run --standalone` could not resolve its server:
#      the child was spawned but its readiness line never reached the parent through the Effect
#      ChildProcessSpawner + Stream.decodeText/splitLines + Deferred path (parent error:
#      `Standalone server exited before reporting readiness`). The same spawn/pipe pattern works on
#      the device with plain node:child_process.spawn (stdin pipe, stdout pipe, stderr inherit or
#      ignore), and `serve --stdio --port 0` directly prints a JSON url line and stays up. The
#      variant therefore uses a direct spawn implementation when process.platform === ios or
#      OPENCODE_IOS=1 (device + host smoke): spawn(executable, [...args, --stdio, --port, 0]), keep
#      the stdin pipe open as the ownership lease, read the first JSON stdout line, retain the child,
#      drain stdout, and enforce a 20s readiness timeout that kills the child and fails clearly.
#      The existing Effect implementation is unchanged for non-iOS platforms.
# Test: OPENCODE_IOS_NODE18=1 bash scripts/build-opencode-bundle.sh build stage smoke manifest;
#       OPENCODE_IOS=1 node opencode.mjs run --standalone ... on host Node 18.20.4, and the device
#       `opencode run --standalone` mock-provider turn.
# Status: iOS device path; behavior on non-iOS is unchanged.

